<http://data.silknow.org/object/ea9ed7ac-2b92-35fc-b332-60fa44b71177>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Ribbon of woven silk taffeta, made by Cox & Co., England, 1851"@en , "Ribbon of woven silk taffeta. White silk tabby ground with a broad tartan satin stripe to either side of the ribbon and made up of differently coloured stripes of varying thickness. A similar broad stripe is made across the ribbon by wefts grouped in the same colour combinations, and bound to give a vertically stripes effect. The colours are royal blue, black, blue-green and pink and red. Label on the back showing the ribbon was exhibited at the 1851 Great Exhibition."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/1531c6cf-1dcf-3c3e-9385-d42235d1c5e1> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/8777587d-0df9-3167-8582-579e8f96a958> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Ribbon of woven silk taffeta. White silk tabby ground with a broad tartan satin stripe to either side of the ribbon and made up of differently coloured stripes of varying thickness. A similar broad stripe is made across the ribbon by wefts grouped in the same colour combinations, and bound to give a vertically stripes effect. The colours are royal blue, black, blue-green and pink and red. Label on the back showing the ribbon was exhibited at the 1851 Great Exhibition."@en , "Ribbon of woven silk taffeta, made by Cox & Co., England, 1851"@en ;
